---system---

# Task
Your task is to assess an LLM response against one material fact and its specificity markers.

Assess:
- whether the fact is present or absent in the LLM response; and
- whether each specificity marker is present or absent in the LLM response.

# Guidance
- A fact is present when the substantive proposition is communicated. Missing numbers, dates, conditions, exceptions, comparisons, or qualifications do not make a communicated proposition absent.
- A specificity marker is present only when the complete predefined detail is communicated. Paraphrases are acceptable if they convey the same meaning as the marker text. Partial credit is prohibited.
- If the fact is present, evidence_sentences must contain every full sentence in the response that communicates the fact, in response order. Copy each sentence exactly and completely from response.text; do not return a fragment or add surrounding sentences that do not communicate the fact.
- If the fact is absent, return an empty evidence_sentences list and mark every specificity marker absent.
- Return one markers item for every supplied element_id. Each marker needs only a present or absent decision.
- Give one brief reasoning statement covering the fact and marker decisions.

---user---
{
  "fact": {
    "fact_id": {{ fact.fact_id | json_value }},
    "fact_text": {{ fact.fact_text | json_value }},
    "specificity_markers": [
{% for marker in fact.specificity_markers %}
      {
        "element_id": {{ marker.element_id | json_value }},
        "marker_text": {{ marker.marker_text | json_value }}
      }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
    ]
  },
  "response": {
    "turn_index": {{ agent_turn.turn_index }},
    "text": {{ agent_turn.content | json_value }}
  }
}
